      "bytes_hex": "08------09------0a------0b------0c",
      "precondition": {
        "before": 3000,
        "after": 3,
        "sha256": "25319904f897d6e189c790747ad70bb90c704b04b3ddb71667377f282a5aec2b"
      },
      "purpose": "The first five entries of the six-entry table that maps the PERFORM screen's BEAT LOOP buttons to the player's list of loop lengths: the buttons that selected 1/2, 1, 2, 4 and 8 beats select 1, 2, 4, 8 and 16 (each 4-byte entry's first byte; `--` keeps the stock bytes between them, unpublished). By static analysis only the BEAT LOOP touch handler reads the table; in emulation it was not read at start-up or in update mode. The sixth entry is the next replacement. The window lies over data before the table (docs/recipes.md, Known exceptions)."
    },
    {
      "offset": 877108,
      "bytes_hex": "0d",
      "precondition": {
        "before": 0,
        "after": 1216,
        "sha256": "1ef2fab950010865b384af1cd2c995d526644ce877dc8f0b01a581c9e743f117"
      },
      "purpose": "The last entry of the BEAT LOOP button table, repeated exactly from beat-loop-16-plays-32.json: the sixth button selects the list's 32-beat entry instead of its 16-beat one. Here that button is relabelled 32 (the image edits)."
    }
  ],
